WEBVTT

00:09.720 --> 00:12.490
Master!

00:40.080 --> 00:43.630
Back then, hadn't Perugius come,

00:43.630 --> 00:46.730
I wouldn't be able to meet
everyone ever again.

00:49.190 --> 00:51.860
Rudy? What's wrong?

00:54.580 --> 00:56.120
It's okay.

01:07.840 --> 01:08.790
Zanoba.

01:08.790 --> 01:10.590
Huh? Master!

01:11.020 --> 01:13.280
Are your wounds okay?

01:13.280 --> 01:14.430
Yeah.

01:14.430 --> 01:16.500
What about you, Zanoba?

01:16.500 --> 01:18.480
As you can see.

01:18.480 --> 01:21.730
I'm sorry for getting you
caught up in my spell.

01:21.730 --> 01:24.740
I'm sure you thought that was
the best course of action.

01:24.740 --> 01:28.960
In that case, let's just celebrate
that we made it back safely.

01:28.960 --> 01:30.210
You're right.

01:30.670 --> 01:33.800
Now, I just hope Nanahoshi's
condition improves.

01:33.800 --> 01:35.700
Nanahoshi will be fine.

01:36.080 --> 01:38.530
Her condition appears
to have stabilized a bit.

01:39.080 --> 01:42.390
I'm more worried about Cliff now.

01:42.390 --> 01:44.620
Is that the demon eye
Kishirika gave you?

01:44.620 --> 01:45.630
Yeah.

01:46.050 --> 01:48.670
Apparently, it's called
the Eye of Identification.

01:49.170 --> 01:52.230
Everything that I see becomes
floating information,

01:52.230 --> 01:54.320
and my vision is filled with text.

01:54.850 --> 01:58.760
I struggled right after
I got the demon eye, too.

01:58.760 --> 02:01.670
Don't worry.
I'll be able to control it in no time.

02:01.670 --> 02:05.520
If anything like this happens again,
you can count on me.

02:05.890 --> 02:06.900
Yes.

02:06.900 --> 02:10.280
If you're going to visit Nanahoshi,
you should go now.

02:10.280 --> 02:12.240
She's probably still awake right now.

02:12.240 --> 02:14.700
Yes, I'll go.

02:17.120 --> 02:24.000
MUSHOKU TENSEI: JOBLESS REINCARNATION SEASON 3

02:34.210 --> 02:35.910
How are you feeling?

02:36.510 --> 02:38.560
I'm feeling a bit better now.

02:38.560 --> 02:42.930
But they told me to rest for
at least another month.

02:43.440 --> 02:46.810
Thank you for saving me.

02:48.290 --> 02:52.460
You went to a dangerous place
to get medicine for me.

02:52.460 --> 02:55.570
So, I'm really grateful to you.

02:56.000 --> 02:58.320
It's unusual for her
to be polite to me.

02:58.690 --> 03:00.380
Don't mind it.

03:00.380 --> 03:02.010
Now that I think about it,

03:02.010 --> 03:06.980
I was acting casual with you,
even though you're older than me.

03:06.980 --> 03:08.500
My apologies.

03:08.500 --> 03:12.170
I don't mind at all.
I'm still eighteen in this world.

03:12.520 --> 03:14.550
How old were you before?

03:14.550 --> 03:19.260
Thirty...
Uh, let's not talk about age.

03:19.260 --> 03:23.020
You don't have to be polite to me,
you can talk like you always have.

03:23.020 --> 03:24.020
Yes.

03:28.390 --> 03:31.520
I'm sure you've already been told
that your illness...

03:31.520 --> 03:33.960
Won't be cured completely, right?

03:35.720 --> 03:40.470
The Sokas Grass can temporarily
break up the mana building inside her,

03:40.470 --> 03:43.620
but mana will accumulate again later.

03:44.000 --> 03:48.750
As long as she's in this world,
she can't avoid mana.

03:50.310 --> 03:53.910
Nanahoshi, you have to return.

03:53.910 --> 03:56.110
You can't die in this world.

03:57.670 --> 03:58.760
Yes...

03:58.760 --> 04:01.050
I'll help you as much as I can.

04:08.740 --> 04:11.070
Thank you very much.

04:14.170 --> 04:16.779
I'll return home.

04:16.779 --> 04:20.660
Of course you want to get back
as soon as you can.

04:20.660 --> 04:22.280
That's not what I meant.

04:22.280 --> 04:24.980
I won't be able to repay you
for everything before I leave.

04:24.980 --> 04:27.240
There's no need to think about that.

04:27.240 --> 04:31.460
But I'd appreciate it if you could give me
advice when I get into trouble.

04:32.250 --> 04:33.460
I understand.

04:35.970 --> 04:39.090
I will leave first.
You have to rest, okay?

04:39.600 --> 04:42.440
Yes, thank you very much.

04:44.470 --> 04:50.600
And that was when my master's purple
light of mana charred Atofe's body.

04:50.600 --> 04:55.710
I see, he was the one
who weakened Atofe like that.

04:55.710 --> 04:58.530
What happened after that?

04:58.530 --> 05:02.470
Unfortunately,
I lost consciousness at that point.

05:02.470 --> 05:04.240
Are you having a tea party?

05:04.240 --> 05:05.500
Master!

05:05.500 --> 05:06.780
That's right.

05:06.780 --> 05:11.540
Lord Perugius said he wanted to know
how our battle with Atofe unfolded.

05:11.540 --> 05:14.520
I was just in the middle of explaining it.

05:14.520 --> 05:16.380
I heard it, Rudeus.

05:16.770 --> 05:21.450
It was your magic that
weakened Atofe so badly.

05:22.600 --> 05:25.760
That sight of her still lingers
in my mind.

05:25.760 --> 05:28.630
Does he really hate her that much?

05:28.630 --> 05:30.180
You seem to be in a good mood.

05:30.180 --> 05:35.590
Because I never expected I would get
an opportunity to take my revenge.

05:35.590 --> 05:37.660
Revenge?

05:37.660 --> 05:38.780
Yes.

05:38.780 --> 05:43.350
She made me suffer countless times
during the Laplace War.

05:43.350 --> 05:46.180
I'd always intended to
take revenge on her,

05:46.180 --> 05:52.500
but then my best friend, North God Kalman,
had forbidden us from killing each other.

05:52.500 --> 05:57.000
Before long, I'd almost given up hope
on taking revenge on her.

05:57.000 --> 06:00.550
But I never imagined I would actually
get to beat her one-sided like that.

06:00.980 --> 06:03.430
I must thank you for that.

06:03.430 --> 06:05.460
You did a great job.

06:05.460 --> 06:08.540
Are you sure it's okay to break
your promise?

06:08.540 --> 06:11.250
Kal forbade us from killing each other.

06:11.250 --> 06:15.020
I'm sure he wouldn't complain
about a one-sided beating.

06:15.020 --> 06:17.940
And she won't die from that much.

06:20.080 --> 06:23.400
It seems I may have misjudged you a bit.

06:23.400 --> 06:26.820
I should give you a reward.

06:26.820 --> 06:28.340
Reward...

06:30.670 --> 06:36.460
Um... Lord Perugius,
could you teach me how to fight?

06:37.680 --> 06:42.420
Are you ignited by your encounter
with Atofe? Or is it just greed?

06:42.420 --> 06:47.930
No... I just want to get strong
enough to protect my family.

06:49.880 --> 06:53.810
For now, I'll give you an item
so that you can contact me.

06:54.290 --> 06:55.550
Sylvaril.

06:58.400 --> 07:01.650
If you use it in any place
that is connected with me,

07:01.650 --> 07:03.800
Clearnight will hear it.

07:03.800 --> 07:06.410
And Almanfi will come to pick you up.

07:06.980 --> 07:10.790
Is he saying that he would come to help
when something happens?

07:10.790 --> 07:13.020
Have a seat too.

07:13.020 --> 07:16.040
Let's continue our chat.

07:16.580 --> 07:21.210
Perugius was actually an interesting
person once you talk to him.

07:21.660 --> 07:25.760
I lack some knowledge,
so I couldn't keep up.

07:25.760 --> 07:29.340
But whenever I heard his story,
my curiosity deepened.

07:29.340 --> 07:30.920
Lord Perugius,

07:30.920 --> 07:35.410
we were thinking of putting the dolls
that Master created on the market soon.

07:35.410 --> 07:38.600
May I ask your opinion on this?

07:40.170 --> 07:44.570
You should have known that
I hate demons.

07:44.570 --> 07:48.240
As expected,
you realize it at first glance.

07:48.800 --> 07:53.400
Zanoba should have known
that Perugius hates demons.

07:53.400 --> 07:54.920
So why is he doing this?

07:54.920 --> 07:58.870
You want to sell this?
Just stop it.

07:59.330 --> 08:05.090
But, Lord Perugius, this doll's model
is someone to whom you owe a debt.

08:05.090 --> 08:06.380
A debt, you say?

08:10.260 --> 08:13.890
Don't tell me,
this is Ruijerd Superdia?

08:13.890 --> 08:16.170
Yes, that's correct.

08:16.170 --> 08:19.860
You've told me before that during
your last battle against Laplace,

08:19.860 --> 08:25.480
it was Sir Ruijerd who assisted you.

08:25.900 --> 08:31.690
Of course, I am aware that
you hate demons.

08:31.690 --> 08:37.409
However, I also believe that my master's
craftsmanship would take the world by storm.

08:37.409 --> 08:43.039
Wouldn't you like to see that happen?
A world overflowing with art.

08:43.039 --> 08:45.450
I hate the Superd.

08:45.450 --> 08:48.380
They killed a lot of innocent lives.

08:48.380 --> 08:53.430
But, it's also true that without
Ruijerd's help, I wouldn't be alive today.

08:53.820 --> 08:55.210
However...

08:57.340 --> 09:01.940
Lord Perugius, Ruijerd regrets
the things he did in the past.

09:01.940 --> 09:03.550
Regret?

09:03.550 --> 09:05.720
He was manipulated by Laplace.

09:05.720 --> 09:10.320
Because of that, he dishonored his tribe
and even killed his own family.

09:10.320 --> 09:12.250
Laplace, huh?

09:12.250 --> 09:14.310
That made him hate Laplace,

09:14.310 --> 09:17.830
and now he's wandering
to restore his tribe's honor.

09:18.240 --> 09:21.580
I made this doll as a way to help him.

09:21.970 --> 09:24.840
I hope you approve our plan,
for his sake too.

09:25.420 --> 09:29.510
I don't care about the Superd's honor.

09:30.120 --> 09:33.220
But I have to repay my debts.

09:33.220 --> 09:35.400
Oh! Then...!

09:35.400 --> 09:37.330
Do as you like.

09:37.330 --> 09:39.430
We appreciate your consideration.

09:39.430 --> 09:42.870
- Lord Perugius, thank you very much!
- Now, we are one step closer

09:42.870 --> 09:44.910
to restoring the Superd honor.

09:44.910 --> 09:47.190
Just wait for it, Ruijerd.

09:47.190 --> 09:48.730
Ah right! Master!

09:48.730 --> 09:52.660
Why don't you show Lord Perugius
how you make dolls?

09:52.660 --> 09:54.440
How do I make dolls?

09:54.440 --> 09:55.690
Show me.

09:55.690 --> 09:58.040
I'm interested in your magic.

09:58.550 --> 10:00.040
I understand.

10:03.170 --> 10:05.300
Is this Sylvaril?

10:05.300 --> 10:09.030
I never thought earth magic
could be used this way.

10:09.030 --> 10:10.300
That's surprising.

10:10.300 --> 10:13.550
If you have a request,
I can make anything you want.

10:13.550 --> 10:17.740
Very well. If you could make
a quality one, bring it to me.

10:17.740 --> 10:19.700
I will buy it from you.

10:19.700 --> 10:21.220
In that case...

10:21.220 --> 10:25.480
We also have some splendid craftsmen
in the Asura Kingdom.

10:25.480 --> 10:30.470
When I become the king, I will have them
make Lord Perugius's statue.

10:31.350 --> 10:36.550
I have no interest in the works created by
craftsmen who sought nobles' satisfaction.

10:37.560 --> 10:41.750
When you become king, you have more
important things to do than that.

10:42.280 --> 10:44.350
T-That is...

10:46.240 --> 10:48.630
Ariel Anemoi Asura.

10:48.630 --> 10:51.550
What does being a king mean to you?

10:51.550 --> 10:54.760
What does a true king possess?

10:54.760 --> 10:56.570
A king...

10:56.570 --> 11:00.440
A king has to be wise,
listen to their ministers,

11:00.440 --> 11:01.970
and never forget their position...

11:01.970 --> 11:03.200
Wrong.

11:03.770 --> 11:07.850
My sworn friend, Gaunis Freean Asura,
was a true king.

11:07.850 --> 11:10.200
But he was nothing like
what you describe.

11:10.200 --> 11:15.540
A coward who hated fighting
and often flirted with women in bars.

11:15.540 --> 11:17.720
He was that kind of man.

11:18.320 --> 11:22.620
But he had the most important
quality of a king.

11:22.620 --> 11:27.790
That's why I believe he's a true king.

11:28.400 --> 11:30.570
What kind of quality was that?

11:30.570 --> 11:35.550
If you can answer that yourself,
I will give you my support.

11:36.100 --> 11:39.550
I see. He's testing Ariel.

11:39.550 --> 11:43.330
Rudeus, what do you think?

11:43.330 --> 11:46.250
What does being a king mean, was it?

11:48.440 --> 11:50.140
In my opinion,

11:50.820 --> 11:56.190
I'd prefer a king who can put themselves
in the shoes of their people.

11:56.190 --> 11:57.270
Oh.

11:58.140 --> 12:01.410
He gave a better answer than you.

12:03.160 --> 12:07.370
Think hard, Ariel Anemoi Asura.

12:11.950 --> 12:16.210
The most important quality as a king...

12:20.460 --> 12:22.010
We're home!

12:22.010 --> 12:24.740
Yes, yes!
Welcome home!

12:24.740 --> 12:25.640
Huh?!

12:26.030 --> 12:28.370
Big Brother and Big Sis Sylphie!

12:28.370 --> 12:29.140
I'm back.

12:29.140 --> 12:31.020
Are you done already?

12:31.020 --> 12:33.400
Did you save Miss Nanahoshi?

12:33.840 --> 12:34.810
Or...

12:34.810 --> 12:37.090
Welcome back, you two.

12:37.090 --> 12:38.420
I'm back.

12:38.420 --> 12:41.300
How are you feeling, Sylphie?

12:41.300 --> 12:44.770
Sorry to make you worry.
I had to stay there for a while.

12:44.770 --> 12:46.080
That's okay.

12:46.080 --> 12:50.960
Actually, the plan was for me
to return home first.

12:50.960 --> 12:54.280
Looks like everything went well.

12:54.280 --> 12:57.510
Yeah, I'll explain that later.

12:57.510 --> 12:59.400
But before I do...

13:01.550 --> 13:03.010
I'm back.

13:04.670 --> 13:06.130
Welcome home.

13:09.460 --> 13:13.270
And that's everything,
Nanahoshi is going to be okay for now.

13:13.270 --> 13:19.090
Still, we only found out that
Mom's condition is related to curses.

13:19.090 --> 13:20.240
I'm sorry.

13:20.660 --> 13:23.200
I think finding that itself
is a great progression.

13:23.620 --> 13:28.600
I'll continue staying at the floating
fortress while looking for the cure.

13:28.600 --> 13:33.120
And I have to stay there as
Princess Ariel's bodyguard.

13:33.120 --> 13:36.710
I understand. There's no need
to worry about the house.

13:37.140 --> 13:38.200
I'm sorry.

13:38.200 --> 13:41.000
We'll return home on the days
when we feel like we can go back.

13:41.000 --> 13:42.900
So, I'm leaving Lucie with you.

13:42.900 --> 13:45.870
Leave it to us to take care of the house.

13:45.870 --> 13:47.470
Thank you very much.

13:49.160 --> 13:50.840
That's the end of our report.

13:50.840 --> 13:52.980
If anything happens,
we'll let you know.

13:57.870 --> 14:03.850
It's only been a few days, but a lot has
happened since we went to meet Perugius.

14:03.850 --> 14:06.850
Nanahoshi collapsed,
then we went to the Demon Continent,

14:06.850 --> 14:10.040
met Kishirika again,
and made Atofe angry.

14:12.530 --> 14:14.040
She was really strong.

14:16.210 --> 14:19.630
I need to become stronger too.

14:20.240 --> 14:26.010
Maybe I was heading in the right direction
by learning from Perugius.

14:27.090 --> 14:29.920
What else was there?

14:31.280 --> 14:36.330
I'm always forgetting older things
when I'm thinking about a lot of things.

14:36.330 --> 14:40.100
If I keep going like this, I might end up
making the same mistakes again.

14:40.660 --> 14:42.900
All right, let's make a diary.

14:42.900 --> 14:44.630
Yeah, let's write!

14:44.630 --> 14:46.240
Let's write right now!

14:57.810 --> 14:58.810
Good.

15:00.550 --> 15:02.800
DIARY
RUDEUS GREYRAT

15:03.410 --> 15:06.430
All right, where should I start?

15:07.020 --> 15:09.680
How long has it been
since I started a diary?

15:09.680 --> 15:10.360
I'VE DECIDED TO START KEEPING A DIARY.

15:10.360 --> 15:13.230
I'VE DECIDED TO START KEEPING A DIARY.
Let's hope I don't quit after just three days.

15:13.230 --> 15:16.690
IT'S BEEN AN EVENTFUL COUPLE OF DAYS...

15:23.410 --> 15:24.440
Heya!

15:25.010 --> 15:26.210
You...

15:26.940 --> 15:29.680
That means I fell asleep?

15:29.680 --> 15:31.110
It's been a while.

15:31.110 --> 15:36.580
Yeah, but when I was an adventurer,
you didn't show your face for three years.

15:37.020 --> 15:39.670
I was pretty messed up back then, too.

15:39.670 --> 15:41.050
That's right.

15:41.050 --> 15:45.840
Compared to back then, you seem
to be doing really well these days.

15:45.840 --> 15:47.290
I guess so.

15:47.290 --> 15:49.850
I got married, and I'm getting
along well with my family.

15:49.850 --> 15:53.740
It's definitely much more fulfilling
than my previous life.

15:53.740 --> 15:56.350
And you got to know Perugius as well.

15:56.350 --> 15:59.390
Perugius, huh?
He is really amazing.

15:59.390 --> 16:01.420
Atofe also took a liking to you.

16:01.420 --> 16:05.530
I kind of wish she didn't.

16:05.530 --> 16:08.130
Hadn't I learned
king-tier water magic from Roxy,

16:08.130 --> 16:09.750
things might've gotten really bad.

16:09.750 --> 16:12.620
It sure was.
That magic you used was amazing.

16:12.620 --> 16:18.620
There isn't much magic out there that can
ignore Battle Aura and paralyze a body.

16:18.620 --> 16:21.080
Battle Aura? What is that?

16:21.080 --> 16:24.050
It's a technique that
uses the mana inside your body

16:24.050 --> 16:26.160
to boost your physical abilities.

16:26.160 --> 16:29.090
If you master it,
you become more agile,

16:29.090 --> 16:32.280
and you won't get hurt by
ordinary attacks.

16:32.280 --> 16:36.530
Apparently, if you train your body enough,
you'll naturally be able to use it.

16:36.530 --> 16:40.980
I've been training pretty hard myself,
but I've never been able to use it.

16:40.980 --> 16:46.190
Sometimes, there are people who can't use
Battle Aura no matter how much they train.

16:46.560 --> 16:48.190
It's down to talent, I guess.

16:48.690 --> 16:50.250
Thanks for pointing it out.

16:50.250 --> 16:52.260
Don't lose heart because of it.

16:52.260 --> 16:55.500
Your magic can ignore Battle Aura.

16:55.500 --> 16:58.340
I'm sure it'll work on Orsted, too.

16:58.340 --> 16:59.910
Is that so?

16:59.910 --> 17:02.980
Hey, I have no interest
in fighting Orsted.

17:02.980 --> 17:04.500
I have nothing against him.

17:04.500 --> 17:05.550
Really?

17:05.550 --> 17:09.750
Anyway, you really helped me
back on the Begaritt Continent.

17:09.750 --> 17:12.560
I'd be lying if I said
I didn't have any regrets.

17:12.560 --> 17:14.780
But it wasn't all bad.

17:14.780 --> 17:17.579
Although I didn't follow
your advice in the end.

17:17.579 --> 17:20.060
Well, that was your choice.

17:20.060 --> 17:22.500
Just out of curiosity,

17:22.500 --> 17:25.020
what would have happened
if I didn't go?

17:25.020 --> 17:26.290
If you didn't go,

17:26.290 --> 17:29.700
your father would have found
some way to save your mother,

17:29.700 --> 17:31.450
and he wouldn't have died.

17:31.450 --> 17:38.350
And you would have lived happily
with two beastfolk princesses.

17:38.350 --> 17:40.190
What the heck?

17:40.190 --> 17:43.370
So you're saying Paul died
because I went there?

17:43.680 --> 17:45.090
That's right.

17:45.090 --> 17:49.290
Because you were there,
he was eager to show off,

17:49.290 --> 17:51.630
and that's the cause of his death.

17:52.060 --> 17:55.140
But, that can't be...

17:55.140 --> 17:59.430
If you ignored it back then,
he would have rescued your mother.

17:59.430 --> 18:01.470
Roxy, too, of course.

18:02.350 --> 18:04.670
I find it hard to believe.

18:04.670 --> 18:06.860
There's no way
it would go that smoothly.

18:06.860 --> 18:08.360
Maybe so!

18:08.360 --> 18:11.320
But that's what we call fate.

18:11.700 --> 18:13.310
I see.

18:13.310 --> 18:16.320
It would've been better
if I didn't go.

18:16.320 --> 18:19.580
Damn it.
Hearing that really gets me down.

18:20.000 --> 18:21.610
It's in the past now.

18:22.500 --> 18:25.830
You're right.
Regrets won't change the past.

18:26.350 --> 18:29.270
Right now, I'm happy.

18:29.270 --> 18:33.340
Although it's true that the choice I made
back then might be a mistake.

18:33.780 --> 18:37.850
I don't think it was all bad.

18:37.850 --> 18:39.380
You sure are optimistic.

18:39.870 --> 18:42.410
Anyway, what is it this time?

18:42.410 --> 18:44.470
Are you going to tell me
some advice again?

18:44.470 --> 18:48.200
No, it's less advice
and more like a favor.

18:48.200 --> 18:50.510
A favor? That's unusual.

18:50.510 --> 18:53.360
Even I sometimes
need to ask for a favor.

18:53.860 --> 18:55.320
Fine.

18:55.320 --> 19:00.580
I think it wouldn't be bad to follow
your advice every now and then.

19:00.580 --> 19:01.970
Oh, really?

19:01.970 --> 19:04.040
I'm happy to hear that.

19:04.040 --> 19:06.830
Well, you have helped me a lot.

19:06.830 --> 19:09.540
In fact, I feel bad
for doubting you before.

19:09.540 --> 19:12.010
Even like this,
I'm still a god, you know.

19:12.010 --> 19:15.630
I don't have a hobby of leading people
astray to take pleasure from their misery.

19:15.630 --> 19:17.040
Sure thing.

19:17.510 --> 19:19.680
So? What do you want from me?

19:19.680 --> 19:21.340
It's nothing big.

19:21.850 --> 19:26.620
I want you to go down to your basement
and check if there's something odd there.

19:26.620 --> 19:30.230
If you don't see anything,
then don't worry about it.

19:30.230 --> 19:33.500
Something odd in the basement?
But why?

19:33.500 --> 19:35.350
Okay, I got it.

19:35.350 --> 19:39.380
I won't question you this time,
and will just do it.

19:40.220 --> 19:41.590
Is that so?

19:47.580 --> 19:49.490
Thank you.

20:00.280 --> 20:02.570
Was it Sylphie? Or maybe Roxy?

20:03.410 --> 20:05.710
They should have woken me up.

20:12.980 --> 20:14.550
All right, then...

20:16.140 --> 20:17.780
So cold.

20:17.780 --> 20:21.020
He told me to check
the basement, I guess?

20:21.020 --> 20:23.030
What weird advice.

20:24.080 --> 20:27.570
Is there something wrong
with my sacred object?

20:27.570 --> 20:29.540
There's no way, right?

20:41.470 --> 20:43.160
Is it just my imagination?

20:45.520 --> 20:47.650
And I got you!

20:47.650 --> 20:49.020
Just kidding...

20:53.340 --> 20:56.480
Was it a success?

20:57.930 --> 21:01.240
No... This is a failure.

21:01.920 --> 21:04.630
I guess there was no way
it could succeed.

21:04.630 --> 21:06.740
W-Who are you?

21:07.590 --> 21:10.040
Are you the Man-God?

21:12.710 --> 21:15.340
Don't go to the basement.

21:15.340 --> 21:18.590
Right now, you've been
deceived by the Man-God.

21:18.590 --> 21:21.020
Hold on a second here.

21:21.020 --> 21:22.910
Who are you?

21:22.910 --> 21:24.720
How did you get in here?

21:25.900 --> 21:27.210
I am...

21:29.920 --> 21:31.480
My name is...

21:36.980 --> 21:41.680
I was the only one in this world
who knew that name.

21:42.560 --> 21:46.740
Until the day I die, I should be
the only one who knows that name.

21:47.090 --> 21:49.200
The name I wanted to forget.

21:49.860 --> 21:53.120
The name that shouldn't exist
in this world.

21:53.630 --> 21:57.380
That was my name from my previous life.

21:58.160 --> 22:02.010
I came from the future.

22:02.010 --> 22:05.010
EPISODE 11
TURNING POINT 4

23:35.010 --> 23:40.020
NEXT EPISODE
AN END AND A BEGINNING
